<h1>About Pokemon Explorer</h1>

<p>Welcome to my Pokemon Explorer app! This is created on Ruby on Rails application
  This displays all the data on Pokemon about there moves, types, pokemon name, pokedex number etc.
  This application was created by myself Trent Taylor and I used multiple data sources to which are down below.
</p>


<h2>Data Sources</h2>

<ul>
  <li> I used PokeAPI to collect the Pokemon details such as types, abilities, weight, hieght, the sprites and the base experience.</li>
  <li>I used the fanzeyi pokemon.json Github dataset as well, the dataset used as a json source for Pokedex informantion. </li>
  <li>Then I just used the faker gem to generate fake reveiws by fake trainers to what they think on the pokemon. </li>
</ul>

<h2>Database Structure</h2>

<p>The databse includes the following tables:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Pokemons</li>
  <li>Types</li>
  <li>Moves</li>
  <li>Abilities</li>
  <li>Reviews</li>
</ul>

<p>This table also contains relationships between the different tables.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Pokemons_Types</li>
  <li>Pokemons_Moves</li>
  <li>Pokemons_Abilities</li>
</ul>

<p>Pokemon can have many types, abilities, moves, and reveiws. Types, abilities, moves, and reviews
  can belong to many pokemons, this is the reason why I created the join tables to connect the relationships between the different tables.
</p>

